{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:19:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_9548086c8d204bf19c0ec746fe647207","id":"pg_034ff0fee7965bea9bea60189547379c","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/microsoft-amplifier-docs-adr-template-md-28588b93886d-60189547379c.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f58fd3507bc8573ab0a44fa3450ce83c"],"title":"microsoft/amplifier/docs/ADR_TEMPLATE.md @ 28588b93886d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:19:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9548086c8d204bf19c0ec746fe647207"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:19:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_9548086c8d204bf19c0ec746fe647207","id":"pg_5cd7815683b458f18b79b73171de17f6","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/microsoft-amplifier-roadmap-md-28588b93886d-b73171de17f6.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_854f45c0313c551a822c1b09a131d6de"],"title":"microsoft/amplifier/ROADMAP.md @ 28588b93886d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:19:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9548086c8d204bf19c0ec746fe647207"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_5f23cd0a1d1cc5075c6b7f5409d2ff64849371e5a57f4c56bc2b863ad3580245"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Providers are switched with commands like 'amplifier provider use openai' or explicit flags such as --model and --deployment; bundles are added and activated with 'amplifier bundle add' and 'amplifier bundle use'."},{"claim_ids":["clm_826e6306bbdac5ac13e2013ae1369de1c5a011ac42d60cea392ddc8e46e0da39"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project builds on separate ecosystem repos: amplifier-core, a roughly 2,600-line kernel providing module protocols, session lifecycle, and hooks, and amplifier-foundation, a bundle composition library plus the default foundation bundle."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a26993efb185ee35ced6adbddb41155da058d46c48382d1e514300c4bc200c94"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Bundles are composable configuration packages defining tools, providers, agents, and behaviors; the default 'foundation' bundle includes filesystem, bash, web, search, and task-delegation tools plus 14 specialized agents."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cab973f079ba450cab067414c89d55ea3da7b9bb45dad0be19eed1dd998e408e"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Supported AI providers include Anthropic Claude (recommended and most tested), OpenAI, Azure OpenAI with managed identity support, and Ollama for local free use; other providers are acknowledged as needing more testing."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d5560c1df3035c0971e1a927de12d61acbb413349ee2fccb3e24ae8cf52713dc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Amplifier is a command-line AI assistant with a modular, extensible architecture; the CLI is described as just one reference interface for the underlying modular platform."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d99c7d6b39df0f0d2203b1679d7f215aae5e97f3991ef53793cbe136a09d03df"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Every interaction is automatically saved and sessions are project-scoped; users can list sessions for the current project or across all projects with 'amplifier session list' and its --all-projects flag."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f2759e7fb0653255324577daf8f08b5de9fe5a0f1806202ae13680385d6d1d50"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is an early research demonstrator with safety systems not yet built in; APIs may change, some features are experimental, and native Windows shells have known issues with WSL recommended instead."},{"claim_ids":["clm_feafbfee899df31c306b17cb804cd51a9f235c122792c03ee0ff551bfe567138"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Chat mode persists context across messages and offers slash commands (/help, /tools, /agents, /status, /config) plus /think and /do to toggle plan mode; single-shot use is via 'amplifier run'."}],"claim_ids":["clm_5f23cd0a1d1cc5075c6b7f5409d2ff64849371e5a57f4c56bc2b863ad3580245","clm_826e6306bbdac5ac13e2013ae1369de1c5a011ac42d60cea392ddc8e46e0da39","clm_a26993efb185ee35ced6adbddb41155da058d46c48382d1e514300c4bc200c94","clm_cab973f079ba450cab067414c89d55ea3da7b9bb45dad0be19eed1dd998e408e","clm_d5560c1df3035c0971e1a927de12d61acbb413349ee2fccb3e24ae8cf52713dc","clm_d99c7d6b39df0f0d2203b1679d7f215aae5e97f3991ef53793cbe136a09d03df","clm_f2759e7fb0653255324577daf8f08b5de9fe5a0f1806202ae13680385d6d1d50","clm_feafbfee899df31c306b17cb804cd51a9f235c122792c03ee0ff551bfe567138"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:19:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_9548086c8d204bf19c0ec746fe647207","id":"pg_6a99110343165e8fb5bea068453861ec","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/microsoft-amplifier-readme-md-28588b93886d-a068453861ec.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_76647e7a95ad50b1a5935bb534ffdf39"],"title":"microsoft/amplifier/README.md @ 28588b93886d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:19:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9548086c8d204bf19c0ec746fe647207"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_34b07f73b02a43578c752819348d39c44dc33ad06275e6004bf563c83c46b3e0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Delegated child sessions resolve their provider by spawn-time precedence: caller provider_preferences, then agent overlay preferences (possibly written from model_role by a routing hook), then parent mount-plan defaults."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d764a6d731b7050577da4e9535a392caad46ed70569d61df72c0fe49b643b2d6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Routing matrices map semantic model roles to ordered provider/model candidates, but routing applies only when the composed bundle mounts a routing strategy such as the routing-matrix hook."},{"claim_ids":["clm_dd0b22ed9f0d7ab2c083cd5146fc9df32524619e98c6b7e4397e831b45158a1f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The architecture distinguishes a provider module (a vendor-protocol adapter) from configured provider instances, so one module can back multiple instances with unique IDs, accounts, models, and priorities."}],"claim_ids":["clm_34b07f73b02a43578c752819348d39c44dc33ad06275e6004bf563c83c46b3e0","clm_d764a6d731b7050577da4e9535a392caad46ed70569d61df72c0fe49b643b2d6","clm_dd0b22ed9f0d7ab2c083cd5146fc9df32524619e98c6b7e4397e831b45158a1f"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:19:10Z","created_by_operation":"op_9548086c8d204bf19c0ec746fe647207","id":"pg_73652a81a92b54bebb3e473f9f6cda49","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/microsoft-amplifier-docs-bundles-providers-routing-projects-md-28588b9-473f9f6cda49.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_59514b538a1a5efd8843e2f8a517943d"],"title":"microsoft/amplifier/docs/BUNDLES_PROVIDERS_ROUTING_PROJECTS.md @ 28588b93886d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:19:10Z","updated_by_operation":"op_9548086c8d204bf19c0ec746fe647207"}
